Patch 0011 (heap_convert.c): superseded; do not apply the original delta.

The authorized supplied AIO fix 0008 already replaced Relation-based conversion
and conversion-time GenericXLog with by-value metadata and BM_CONVERTED.
Every converted buffer is marked for a full image on later WAL registration;
this covers double-xmax conversion without WAL insertion in an AIO worker.
Restoring patch 0011 would reintroduce obsolete conversion-time WAL behavior.

Remaining review: supplied fix 0015 ensures converted images override NO_IMAGE
and preserves conversion markers on NO_CHANGE references. PG19 moved visibility
logging into prune WAL, so its heap-LSN rule must be adapted in pruneheap.c.
The original patch remains preserved under pg19xid64v67/.
